<section class="featured" id="systems">
  <div class="section-heading"><p>FEATURED PROJECTS</p><h2>Selected projects.</h2><span>Each project starts with a real need and shows how I turned the workflow into a solution people can use.</span></div>
  <div class="featured-list">
    <article class="feature-case feature-case--reverse"><div class="feature-case__copy"><div class="case-index"><span>01</span><span class="status status--internal">INTERNAL USE</span></div><p class="case-category">Technical documents · local translation</p><h3>Offline Document Translator</h3><p class="case-summary">I built a desktop app that translates Word and ODT documents without pulling apart tables, images or formatting.</p><div class="case-impact"><small>Use</small><strong>People across different company areas prepare technical material in Portuguese and English, review it and can create a bilingual PDF.</strong></div><p class="case-stack">Python · PySide6 · DOCX/ODT · local translation · Windows</p><div class="project-links"><a class="text-link" href="cases/offline-document-translator/">See how it works<span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></div></div><div class="feature-case__visual"><figure class="case-showcase"><div class="case-showcase__frame"><img src="../assets/evidence/tradutor-interface-bilingue.png" alt="The translator showing a completed demonstration document and bilingual output." loading="eager" decoding="async"></div><figcaption><span class="evidence-label">REAL INTERFACE · DEMONSTRATION DOCUMENT</span><strong>Document ready for translation.</strong></figcaption></figure></div></article>

    <article class="feature-case feature-case--producao feature-case--reverse"><div class="feature-case__copy"><div class="case-index"><span>02</span><span class="status status--production">IN OPERATION</span></div><p class="case-category">Windows application · manufacturing · tracking</p><h3>Production Operations</h3><p class="case-summary">I deployed an application to organize production orders and share updates across the office, factory and a TV panel.</p><div class="case-impact"><small>In practice</small><strong>Office and production teams follow orders through a shared view.</strong></div><p class="case-stack">Python · PySide6 · SQLite · Windows</p><div class="project-links"><a class="text-link" href="cases/producao-operacional/">See how it works<span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a><a class="text-link text-link--muted" href="https://github.com/Mayconxzdev/ProducaoOperacional">View code<span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></div></div><div class="feature-case__visual"><div class="visual visual--production"><div class="deployment-map"><div class="node"><small>OFFICE</small><b>Orders</b><span>entry and follow-up</span></div><div class="line"></div><div class="branches"><div class="node node--core"><small>SHARED WORKFLOW</small><b>Production</b><span>organized updates</span></div><div class="node"><small>FACTORY</small><b>Panel</b><span>shared view</span></div></div></div></div></div></article>

    <article class="feature-case feature-case--proposta-comercial"><div class="feature-case__copy"><div class="case-index"><span>03</span><span class="status status--internal">INTERNAL USE</span></div><p class="case-category">Documents · commercial process · email</p><h3>Commercial Proposal</h3><p class="case-summary">I built a workflow that brings requests, commercial templates, document generation and customer communication together.</p><div class="case-impact"><small>In practice</small><strong>The team prepares and reviews the proposal, then sends the email from the app after approval.</strong></div><p class="case-stack">Python · PySide6 · SQLite · ODT/PDF · IMAP/SMTP</p><div class="project-links"><a class="text-link" href="cases/commercial-proposal/">See how it works<span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></div></div><div class="feature-case__visual"><div class="visual visual--proposals"><div class="compare-column"><span>REQUEST</span><strong>Template</strong></div><div class="compare-arrow">→</div><div class="compare-column compare-column--after"><span>REVIEW</span><strong>Send</strong></div><div class="compare-footer"><span>real templates</span><span>human approval</span></div></div></div></article>

    <article class="feature-case feature-case--postagem-redes"><div class="feature-case__copy"><div class="case-index"><span>04</span><span class="status status--pilot">FUNCTIONAL DEMO</span></div><p class="case-category">Applied AI · content automation</p><h3>Postagem Redes</h3><p class="case-summary">I built an automation that drafts content from approved context and keeps each channel’s workflow separate.</p><div class="case-impact"><small>In practice</small><strong>Content goes through human review before anything is published to social networks.</strong></div><p class="case-stack">n8n · APIs · RAG/grounding · OAuth2</p><div class="project-links"><a class="text-link" href="cases/postagem-redes/">See how it works<span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a><a class="text-link text-link--muted" href="https://github.com/Mayconxzdev/PostagemRedes">View code<span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></div></div><div class="feature-case__visual"><div class="visual visual--social"><div class="publication-flow"><span>Context</span><i>→</i><span>Draft</span><i>→</i><span>Review</span><i>→</i><span>Publish</span></div><div class="visual-facts"><span>human approval</span><span>separate channel flows</span></div></div></div></article>
  </div>
</section>
